WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.835
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Ethan Hawke.

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.603
You have scooched over a little.
-I have. I'm sorry I encroached.

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:06.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a little bit like havin
a chaperone at a date.

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:08.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, like in high school.
You know, you had to --

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:10.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And we're -- you know,
obviously we're working out.

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:11.911
You did get a COVID test,
which we appreciate...

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did, yeah.
-...in order for you

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:14.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
to come into the studio,
you had to do that,

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.717
and we did have our -- you know,
we're very lucky to have peopl

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:18.785
who are keeping an eye on things
for us.

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.820
And they did come out during the
commercial break and said like

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I think maybe one more."
-I appreciate that.

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:24.057 line:92%
-Yeah, exactly. Safety first

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:26.760
So, you know, I feel like we
all, you know, there's maybe

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.195
at least one paragraph
in American history books

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:29.763 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
about John Brown.

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:32.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
Harper's family --
Harper's Ferry, excuse me.

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:32.799 line:92%
We could tick those boxes.

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:36.970
James McBride made this really
interesting choice in his book

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.105 size:88% position:44%
There's a lot of levity.
There's a lot of humor

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:42.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
that comes through
in the series as well.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:44.310 size:78% position:39%
Did you though think,
"Oh, this is so cool

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.813
that I get to not just tel
the story of James Brown --"

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:48.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sorry, John Brown.
-James Brown.

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:49.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
That would be
a good movie too.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:51.551
-Why wasn't James Brown in this?
I don't know much about history.

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:52.585 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I don't know!

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:54.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But you get to tell
the John Brown --

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.723
not the history books versio
but the James McBride version,

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
which seems like it must hav
been a lot more fun.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:01.061 line:92%
-That's the reason to do it.

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:02.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nobody really wants to
be taught.

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:05.765
I mean, as much as we all like
our local librarian, you know,

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's not what
you tune in for movies.

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-You want to be entertained.

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:11.871 size:84% position:42%
And what McBride did is
pull off a magic trick,

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:16.376
which is to talk about some of
this nation's greatest pains

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:17.277 line:92%
some of its greatest hurts

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:21.781
and to do it with so much wi
and love that it disarms you

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:24.417
You know, you're used to
feeling like if you have t

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:27.921
look at this, you know,
dark part of U.S. history

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:31.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you're going to --
that it's just going to hurt

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:34.861
And it does hurt,
but he does it with so much love

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:37.263
that it hurts in a way
that is healing, I found.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:40.033
I mean, when I was first reading
the book, I was sitting ther

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.935
in my bed and I'm just laughing,
you know?

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:45.171
I keep cackling, and my wife's
like, "What are you reading?

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.173 size:78% position:39%
And I said, you know,
"The Good Lord Bird."

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she's like,
"Isn't that about John Brown?"

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:49.709 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm like, "I know!"

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:52.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause it's kind of as if --
I don't know --

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:55.115
Chris Rock, Redd Foxx,
or Richard Pryor told you

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:56.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
the story of John Brown.
-Yeah.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.184 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-You know, it's not --

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:00.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
It has an incendiary quality
to it.

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:06.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think that, as you know,
humor is a great teacher.

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:07.727 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Humor doesn't lie.

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:09.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, when your body
just laughs,

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:10.964 line:92%
your brain doesn't laugh.

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:14.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you don't have
a political attack on it.

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:17.770
You just have an emotional human
hit on the story.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:20.740 size:81% position:41%
So that's absolutely
why I wanted to do it.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:24.210
-And then, obviously, you pu
together an incredible cast,

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
which this has
up and down the board.

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:29.782 size:84% position:42%
And one cast member,
obviously close to you,

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:32.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
we've talked about her before,
your daughter Maya,

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:33.453 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
was in it as well.

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:35.822
I mean, it must be so fun
to get to work with her,

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
not just because
she's your daughter

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:38.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
but because of
her immense talent.

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:42.929 size:84% position:42%
-Well, it's a little
mind-blowing, you know?

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:46.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
People are often all over
the Internet and news

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:49.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
and TV shows and stuff,
you know, trying to stay young

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:53.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
trying to talk about
how awful it is getting old.

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:57.210
And then you find yourself
on a set, telling a story

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.612
that you really want to tell
that you have a passion to tell,

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:04.217
and your 22-year-old daughte
wants to tell it with you.

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:06.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she's got ideas
and she has --

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:10.256
she has a grace that she gav
the show that I didn't kno

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:11.324 size:88% position:44% line:92%
that we needed so badly.

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:15.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
The funny thing about it
was that I really wanted May

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:17.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
to play this part,
and I was kind of scared

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:19.732
to bring it up with her and kind
of scared to bring it up

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.467
with Showtime because I wa
worried they would think

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:24.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was just
a crazy, nepotistic dad,

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:27.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so I was like,
"How am I gonna bring this up?

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:28.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then "Stranger Things"
came out.

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:31.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then somebody from Showtim
called, "Hey, you know,

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:32.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're looking at
the part of your daughter.

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:36.549
I mean, would your actual
daughter be interested?"

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.952 line:92%
"Oh, what a fascinating idea!"

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:40.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha!
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:41.387 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You know?

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so it all just
kind of fell into place,

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:46.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they were glad to have her
and I was glad to have her

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:47.694 line:92%
and she was happy to be there.

00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:51.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You seem to have a closenes
with all your kids.

00:03:51.564 --> 00:03:53.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
It must help
when you're actually on se

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:55.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it doesn't seem like -
I don't know --

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:58.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you're an intimidatin
father figure that --

00:03:58.438 --> 00:03:59.472 line:92%
-I try to be intimidating.

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:01.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
Yeah, it just doesn't take

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:02.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I've seen
all your kids with you.

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:03.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
They do not seem
even the littlest --

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:06.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not a little intimidated?
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:07.347 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-I'll tell you this.

00:04:07.347 --> 00:04:09.315 line:92%
With all my kids this is true,

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:14.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
but Maya is the oldest,
and so I know it more deeply

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:16.522
I've been working with May
since she was a little girl.

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:19.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's an incredibly --
She has an album out right now

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:20.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
called "Blush"
if anybody wants to get it

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:23.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's a really gifted youn
woman, and she always has been

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:26.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we used to work on
watercolors, and she would say

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:27.934 line:92%
"Oh, I don't really like that.

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think
that's too much red?

00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:32.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think that looks more
like a dog or a bird?

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:34.340 line:92%
Hmm, let's switch it out."

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.975 line:92%
But she's always been gifted

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:39.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we've always had
an easy dialogue about art

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:43.983
I think one of the things that
was most difficult about her

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:48.121 line:92%
being on set was asking myself

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:51.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Am I the actor
I told her I was?"

00:04:51.124 --> 00:04:51.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know?
-Oh, right.

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:52.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you know what I mean?
Here I've been --

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:55.094
For years, I've been telling her
to respect acting.

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:55.995 line:92%
I'm giving her Uta Hagen's book.

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:58.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm talking to her
about what is an actor.

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:00.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
What does it mean?
Because the world tells yo

00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:03.202
one thing that it is, but fo
the people who really do it,

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:07.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
who are committed to
storytelling and committed t

00:05:07.307 --> 00:05:10.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
being inside the metaphor
of a play,

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:12.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's a little bit
more mysterious.

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:15.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I had to be the person -
You know?

00:05:15.615 --> 00:05:17.950
Every time I go to the craft
service table, I'd be like

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:20.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
"A real actor doesn't need
this many gummi bears!"

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.722 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:22.722 --> 00:05:24.357 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Anyway, it was great.

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:25.725 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-It turned out great.

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:27.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for making the trip.

00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:31.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
I look forward to seeing you
outside of here soon.

00:05:31.064 --> 00:05:31.764 line:92%
Always a pleasure, Ethan.

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:33.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, thanks.
I'm sorry I had to sit so far.

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:35.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe on our second date
I get to go to here

00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:37.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
and if things go really well
a third, here.

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:38.538 size:81% position:41%
-Yeah, I'm very much
looking forward to it.

00:05:38.538 --> 00:05:41.407
We're getting the thumbs-u
from the staff over there.

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:42.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
The finale of
"The Good Lord Bird"

00:05:42.709 --> 00:05:45.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
airs this Sunday at 10:00 p.m.
on Showtime.

